 sneakers. She holds a Reverse Warrior Pose (Viparita Virabhadrasana) with her right knee bent forward, left leg extended straight back, right arm reaching overhead in a gentle backbend, and left arm extended back at hip level. Soft golden-hour sunlight filters through the trees across the calm lake, casting a warm glow on her face as she breathes slowly with a serene expression. The camera holds a static wide shot. [Shot 2] At 00:02.000, the shot cuts to a medium-wide shot as she flows into Warrior III (Virabhadrasana III): she brings both hands together in prayer at her chest, shifts her weight onto her right leg, hinges forward at the hips, and lifts her straight left leg behind her until her torso and left leg are parallel to the ground, arms now extended straight forward toward the lake. The camera holds a static medium-wide shot, capturing her horizontal balance against the shimmering water and trees. [Shot 3] At 00:04.000, the shot cuts to a full-body shot as she transitions into Dancer's Pose (Natarajasasana): from Warrior III she lowers her left foot briefly to the grass, then bends her left knee to lift the foot behind her, reaches back with her left hand to grasp her left ankle, and extends her right arm straight forward toward the lake as she kicks her left foot into her hand, arching her spine into a graceful standing backbend. She holds the final arched pose with a soft smile, the sunlight catching the side of her face and the cream fabric of her outfit. The camera holds a static full-body shot, ending on her balanced dancer's pose.\n\noverall_soundscape: A gentle breeze rustles the grass and leaves along the shore while soft water lapping at the bank is heard in the background. The woman's steady breathing cycles slowly across the sequence, and the soft thud of her sneakers pivoting on the grass accompanies each pose transition.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A minimal ambient arrangement at a slow tempo, layering sustained piano notes with a low, warm cello 